---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Architecture | Orion Astro MPA Islands Starter"
  description="Multi-page route architecture using native CSS View Transitions and 0 KB client JavaScript."
  activeNav="architecture"
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl space-y-6">
    <p
      class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-[var(--color-orion-fg-muted)]"
      style="font-family: var(--font-orion-mono);"
    >
      Static Route 02
    </p>
    <h1
      class="text-4xl font-bold leading-tight text-white"
      style="font-family: var(--font-orion-display);"
    >
      Native MPA View Transitions Without Client Routers
    </h1>
    <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-orion-fg-muted)]">
      This route emits zero JavaScript bundles. Cross-document navigation uses standard CSS @view-transition rules guarded by prefers-reduced-motion.
    </p>
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-orion-border)] bg-[var(--color-orion-surface)] p-5">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white" style="font-family: var(--font-orion-display);">
        When to Hydrate an Island
      </h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-sm text-[var(--color-orion-fg-muted)]">
        <li>Use static Astro components for articles, monographs, pricing grids, and navigation.</li>
        <li>Add client:visible or client:load only for stateful sandboxes, charts, or calculators.</li>
        <li>Keep per-island hydrated JS strictly under budget.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
